ent JB Pritzker (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Illinois' governor's race is a rematch of 2022, with incumbent Democrat JB Pritzker seeking a third term against Republican Darren Bailey, a downstate former state senator, plus a minor independent candidate. Pritzker enters with the advantages of incumbency, deep personal wealth, and a state that leans Democratic by about six points. He has been on offense, airing attacks on Bailey while also spending to help Democrats elsewhere, including in the Texas governor's race.\n\nRaters unanimously classify the race as Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets price Pritzker's chances at 97 to 98 percent. The limited public polling shows Pritzker ahead by roughly twenty points, consistent with his 2022 result. Bailey has struggled to stay on message under sustained attack, and even some Republican figures have crossed party lines to endorse the incumbent. The race is not competitive in any meaningful sense.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.98, "margin": 13.88}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9829, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.983, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9789, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9753, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9721, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9755, "margin": 13.9}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9748, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9823, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9825, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9825, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9786, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9788, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9803, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9741, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9899, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9923, "margin": 15.0}]}